{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpkrbogp9hqhXxdAJN8t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No. Workers only receive inbound traffic as HTTP(S) requests, including WebSocket upgrades. You can't bind a Worker to port 5432 or have it accept raw TCP from a client like `psql`.\n\nThe TCP support Workers do have goes the other way: the `connect()` API from `cloudflare:sockets` lets a Worker open TCP connections *to* something else, such as a Postgres database. Hyperdrive builds on that to give Workers pooled, accelerated Postgres access. To proxy inbound raw TCP through Cloudflare, you'd use Spectrum (mostly an Enterprise product), which forwards TCP to an origin server you run, not to a Worker. Cloudflare Tunnel is another way to reach a private Postgres server.\n\nThis is from my own knowledge (cutoff mid-2026), not checked against current docs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2464,"cache_read_input_tokens":1693,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2464},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebe226c9-c3f4-45b0-a857-c6043958c14f","uuid":"a01661aa-679b-4989-b2c7-981b45916bbc","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:18:33.860Z","request_id":"req_011CfpkrbWaP9yZPyv3wLuKb"}
